---
subject: Two-factor authentication enabled for {Email}
layout: _Layouts/Base
---
@model Contoso.Emails.TwoFactorEnabledModel

<div class="alert-banner alert-success">
    Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) is now active on your account.
</div>

<Heading Level="1">Two-Factor Authentication Active</Heading>
<p>Hello @Model.Name,</p>
<p>Two-factor authentication using <strong>@Model.AuthMethod</strong> was successfully enabled for <strong>@Model.Email</strong> on @Model.EnabledDate.</p>
<p>From now on, you will be prompted for an authentication code when signing into your Contoso workspace from a new device.</p>

<Spacer Height="16" />
<table border="0" cellpadding="12" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="background:#f8fafc;border-left:4px solid #3b82f6;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:20px;">
    <tr>
        <td>
            <strong>Important reminder:</strong> Store your recovery backup codes in a safe place. If you lose access to your primary device, backup codes are the only way to recover account access.
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<Spacer Height="16" />
<Button Href="@Model.SecuritySettingsUrl" BgColor="#0f172a">View Security Settings</Button>
<Spacer Height="20" />
<Divider />
<p style="font-size: 13px; color: #64748b;"><T.Try Key="security.notice" /></p>

